body:
@nubels thanks for doing some testing, much appreciated!

> After clicking outside of the game window, it sometimes registers input that isn't there. In this clip, I stop pressing A around the 5s mark and my character still moves to the left. After pressing A again, it seems to stop. I'm using Input.get_vector

That doesn't surprise me, as I still have to fine-tune how events are handled as focus enters and leaves the game area, which is currently determined by the mouse. At the moment, events are not sent to the child process if the mouse leaves the game rectangle area. It likely needs to be similar to what happens when you click on a button and move outside, where the tracking is still grabbed by the button.

@nubels 

> On Windows, when you change the window mode to something other than windowed at runtime, you get a message saying Embedded window only supports Windowed mode. This message doesn't seem to appear here.

I can add a log for that, but it is just ignored if you try

@KoBeWi and @AThousandShips thanks for the code reviews – I've pushed all the recommended changes.

@Calinou thanks for the thorough review. I've concluded that we will have to disable embedding in **single-window** mode, as it won't work, for the same reasons it doesn't on Linux and Windows. The OS window manager is compositing the embedded window onto Godot, which means Godot content will render _under_.

I will review your other issues and report back / add fixes.

@Calinou 

> I noticed the CLI arguments used by the embedded process are `--display-driver embedded` `--embedded`. Can `--embedded` imply `--display-driver embedded` so you don't need to use both?

💯 agree. I've made that change.

No stress, @Repiteo! I do have some follow up fixes that I'll prep today in a new PR!

Thanks @akien-mga and to all those that reviewed. 

@Calinou my changes will include preventing embedding in single-window mode.
